 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOAuth2 metadata endpoint returns incorrect response_types_supported\n\n#### Description\n\nThe metadata endpoint is returning an incorrect list for `response_types_supported`. Instead of returning the supported response types (like \"code\" and \"token\"), it's filtering to only include \"none\" which is typically not a valid response type for most OAuth2 flows.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2 import Server\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.endpoints.metadata import MetadataEndpoint\n\n# Create a server endpoint\nendpoint = Server(None)\n\n# Create metadata endpoint with standard configuration\nmetadata = MetadataEndpoint([endpoint], {\n    'issuer': 'https://foo.bar',\n    'authorization_endpoint': 'https://foo.bar/authorize',\n    'token_endpoint': 'https://foo.bar/token'\n})\n\n# Check what response types are supported\nprint(\"Response types supported:\", metadata.claims.get('response_types_supported'))\n# Expected: ['code', 'token'] or similar valid response types\n# Actual: ['none'] or empty list\n```\n\nThe metadata endpoint should return valid OAuth2 response types like \"code\" and \"token\" in the `response_types_supported` field, but it's currently filtering these out and only including \"none\".\n</issue>\n",
